<header><p class="enc-kicker"><a href="/encyclopedia/conflicts/18th-century-bce">Conflicts &amp; Resolutions</a> · Siege</p><h1 class="enc-title">Destruction of Eshnunna</h1><p class="enc-meta"><span class="dates">c. 1755 BCE</span> · <a href="/centuries/18th-century-bce">18th century BCE</a></p></header>
<div class="enc-body"><p class="enc-desc">The destruction of <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/eshnunna">Eshnunna</a> was the final defeat of the Mesopotamian city-state of Eshnunna by <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/hammurabi">Hammurabi</a> of the Babylonian Empire around 1755 BCE. According to the account, it was achieved by damming the city's water supply rather than by direct assault, an example of <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/ecological-warfare">ecological warfare</a> that ruined its agricultural base.</p></div>
